2025:
Mes Aides (https://mes-aides.francetravail.fr/) is a service developed by France Travail, the French national agency for employment, that helps people facing social obstacles (mobility, childcare, access to housing, health, etc.) find human, material and financial assistance to facilitate their path to employment. It is a platform that makes visible and accessible all services available to jobseekers to look for, find and keep a job by overcoming the social obstacles they face. The service attracts 80 000 visitors on average every month. 
Reused open dataset : https://www.data.gouv.fr/fr/datasets/referentiel-de-loffre-dinsertion-sociale-et-professionnelle-data-inclusion/ 
2024:
We focused on two services that converge towards job creation and access:

La Bonne Alternance

La Bonne Alternance is a digital public service that facilitates the connection between young people, apprenticeship training centers (CFA), and companies. Its features include:
- A service for posting job offers accessible to small and medium-sized enterprises (SMEs) and CFAs;
- A service for connecting young people with CFAs;
- A service for sending applications;
- Modules for supporting contact with a CFA, searching for a host company, etc.

The tool relies on data from apprenticeship training offers and job offers. Since the beginning of 2024:

- 12,171 job offers have been posted;
- 538,745 applications have been sent;
- 48,942 contacts with CFAs have been made.

Emplois de l’inclusion

Developed by the GIP de l’inclusion, "Les emplois de l’inclusion" is a service that utilizes open employment data and connects job seekers with social enterprises. It enables the most vulnerable individuals to gain access to employment and training, facilitating their integration into society through work. Through this service:

- 1,150,687 candidates have been hired;
- 5,386 social enterprises have recruited.

Link to the report : https://www.data.gouv.fr/fr/datasets/r/b647386b-b143-4fa3-891e-1ad9d31a19ab

2025:
The majority of responsible institutions have been identified and involved in the process, as well as the maority of the datasets have been mapped, and to some extent openned. Following the first reporting on February 2025, updates were conducted and the report was update several times, to include newly open data. Information sessions were held at both decision-making and technical level and orientations are available. 
Furthermore, the Strategy for Open Data includes actions to further improve the legal framework at national level on this subject. (https://data.gov.ro/pages/hvds; https://data.gov.ro/blog/odd-2025-intalnirea-tehnica-privind-implementarea-regulamentului-hvds)
2024:
There are a series of measures taken, such as:
- SGG has requested the institutions under the scope of the regulation to designate stewards for the implementation (partially appointed);
- SGG has started working groups with the appointed stewards to work on the mapping of datasets and identify the measured needed for implementation (cadastre, meteorological, statistics etc.);
- the appointed stewards are kept updated on implementation and monitoring news from EU level;
- the SGG has participated in the high-level meetings of the Inspire Implementation National Council to inform and foster on the additional measures required for HVDs Regulation in relation to INSPIRE;
- some of the institutions under the scope of the Regulation have initiated impact studies and procedures for the implementation (National Meteorological Authority; National Cadastre Agency);
