2024:
In addition to existing measures:
- the Secretariat-General of the Government is also currently conducting a survey on the portal that also includes questions for collecting examples of data re-use (https://forms.gle/6rMkWhmxLfMyd4nq5);
- the draft secondary legislation includes templates for the yearly reporting that mandates the institutions to also monitor re-use through various approaches (https://e-consultare.gov.ro/w/wp-content/plugins/download-attachments/includes/download.php?id=50045; https://e-consultare.gov.ro/w/hotarare-a-guvernului-pentru-aprobarea-normelor-metodologice-de-aplicare-a-legii-nr-179-2022-privind-datele-deschise-si-reutilizarea-informatiilor-din-sectorul-public/);
- when organising events (webinars, public meetings etc.) the SGG also collects re-use examples from participants and promotes those showcases (https://data.gov.ro/blog/rezumatul-intalnirii-publice-ziua-datelor-deschise-deschiderea-datelor-geospatiale);
- the SGG also maintains constant dialogue with re-users.
2023:
Re-use examples can be submitted through the Contact form (https://data.gov.ro/contact-us) or directly via email and are published by the portal team, following validation on https://data.gov.ro/showcase.

Improving metadata and data quality;
Implementing the arrangements set out in the Open Data Directive and in the HVD Regulation
Using a common licensing framework;

Guidelines for the implementation of the Legislative Decree no. 36/2006 (amended by the Legislative Decree no. 200/2021 transposing the Directive 2019/1024), see https://www.agid.gov.it/sites/default/files/repository_files/lg-open-data_v.1.0_1.pdf;

Regular contacts and support by AgID;

Webinar series (https://dati.gov.it/formazione-su-opendata);

The portal is promoted in several ways:
- it is referenced in the AgID official web sites;
- it is denoted as a tool for users and PAs in the Three-Year Plan for ICT in PA;
- it is denoted as single access point to Open Data in the Legislative Decree No. 36/2006 (amended by the Legislative Decree No. 200/2021 transposing Open Data Directive);
- in national, regional or local events with dedicated presentations, mentions or communication. An example is the Forum PA 2023, the most important national event dedicated to the topic of PA modernisation, where dedicated cards about the national portal were produced, published and distributed to the participants visiting the AgID stand (https://www.facebook.com/photo/?fbid=620067630151604&set=t.100064451182098);
- by launching information campaign oh the web (e.g. https://www.facebook.com/photo/?fbid=767371235421242&set=pb.100064451182098.-2207520000)

The decision to define a national profile (for Italy DCAT-AP_IT)) is mainly due to the needs related to the national legal system. The main extensions introduced concern:
-	The additional mandatory property rightsholder;
-	The additional optional properties subtheme and creator;
-	The class Distribution is mandatory;
-	Changes in the cardinality of several properties (from optional or recommended to mandatory), such as frequency, theme, modified.

Our national extension is documented together with others in DCAT-AP implementation guidelines WG  https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1SPfA6fA9im_6EtxLDBtCMyBpt1q1aXl5ng4epLgSyJM/edit#gid=0

The national profile is available here:
https://docs.italia.it/italia/daf/linee-guida-cataloghi-dati-dcat-ap-it/it/stabile/index.html

.- Controlled vocabularies not used;
.- not appropriate configuration of the technologies used; 
.- mandatory properties missing

.- The Web Analytics Italia platform allows to track the users' access to the national Open Data portal and to other local Open Data portals (https://webanalytics.italia.it/ - it requires authentication);

.- The Torino Municipality Open Data Portal http://aperto.comune.torino.it/dataset collects automated feedback and shows the analytics about views and downloads

- In order to map which and how open data are reused, Regione Puglia has implemented an automated mechanism on the dati.puglia.it portal that keeps track, at a statistical level, of how datasets have been viewed or downloaded, along with other statistical data that are available in the statistics section.

The process is conducted at public body level.
Example:
Lombardia Region collects information about the cases of re-use of the datasets published in the regional data portal and classifies them on base of the scope of the app or service developped, i.e. data journalism, around me (location), B2B services, B2C services, data analysis, ...  (https://www.dati.lombardia.it/Government/Utilizzo-dei-dataset/m58v-fh6e/data);

2025:
Resolution № 835 establishes among other things Principles For Improved Governance & Citizen Engagement and For Inclusive Development & Innovation. The last is defined as granting by data providers support and assistance in creating new information resources and services based on Open Data. It also sets definition of a term "permanent applicability" - ensuring the use of Open Data by public authorities and local governments in the exercise of their powers.
Perfomance of the Principle For Improved Governance & Citizen Engagement of Open Data Strategy provides for:
Promotion of the use of the Open Data by public bodies;
Cooperation with NGOs and business on the creation and promotion of visualizations, tools and analytical materials based on Open Data;
Promotion of the development of skills in the use of Open Data by NGOs and other civil society organisations. Organization of informational and educational activities for the leadership of public authorities and local governments on the development of the effective Open Data programs in their government bodies.
In addition, the draft of the Strategy for the development of Open Data for 2025-27 provides for the provision that the revision of the current legislation on Open Data, including legislative acts regulating, in particular, the reuse of data, should become a key stage in the implementation of the Strategy. In order to implement this task, it is planned to prepare systemic changes to the legislation to eliminate obstacles to access to public information and its use as Open Data. Reuse will also be ensured by increasing the quality, interoperability, quantity and completeness of Open datasets and associated metadata, which is Strategic Goal 2. https://data.gov.ua/uploads/files/2025-05-01-150336.772070OD-Strategy.pdf 
