2025:
The National Digital Strategy also includes the Digital and Smart Nation initiative, which foresees the implementation of platforms to improve urban management and the sharing of territorial data.
In a rapidly evolving world, where global competitiveness and the well-being of populations increasingly depend on robust digital infrastructures, it is necessary to position Portugal as an international reference in connectivity and territorial intelligence, promoting a truly digital and intelligent nation.
This initiative emerges as a strategic response to the need to expand access to intelligent land management solutions, as well as to improve interconnection between different territories, creating an ecosystem of good practices and data sharing.
Within the scope of this initiative, a set of targeted and collaborative actions and interventions are planned between public and private entities and civil society, namely:
• Implementation of Urban Management Platforms at the service of municipalities;
• Implementation of 5 Digital Twins in strategic areas at a national level;
• Development of the Smart Territories Portal;
• Implementation of the Public Policy Dashboard and the Local Government Observatory;
• Implementation of the National Data Management System for Smart Territories;
• Promotion of training sessions, reaching 650 Public Administration workers (already reached).
